Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-14-2001||08:46 PM||||I was letting my car idle when I was working on my fuel canister problem.... When I noticed that my windshield was syeamed up in the middle above the defrost dash vent...  and the lil' square door window vent'shad steam coming from them.  What in the world is causing this now??  Heater Core???  <BR>Thank's for any help...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-14-2001||09:35 PM||||All I can think of is there could have been some condensation (a lot of it) on your heater core, and then once it got warm (hot, actually) it turned to steam.  Did you notice if the engine was running really hot?<BR>  It wasnt smoke right, no burning smell.  Hopefully not.<P>Anyway, that's my idea.  More in likely, you'll have to take a look at the heater core, just to see whats going on.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-14-2001||09:55 PM||||Thank's Joe.....<BR> What is the EASIEST way to get to it to take a look???  <BR>No nothing burning smell at all !!! This car that I'm rebuilding sat on the side of the road for 4 year's...  The inspection on this SE/GT say's 1996...  So what you were saying about the condensation on the heater core might be right....   Thank's again!!Steve<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||01-14-2001||10:25 PM||||Steve,<P>Does the vapor from the defroster smell like antifreeze (a dead giveaway)?<P>I would suggest you do a search on "heater core".  There have been lots of posts describing how to change a heater core, where to by one, etc.  If you remove the heater core cover and antifreeze comes dripping out of the heater box, you found the problem!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-15-2001||11:37 PM||||Mark,   Thank's I'll try to remove the box and see....<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-16-2001||02:13 AM||||In the spots that fogged up, do they feel greasy? Do they smell like antifreeze? It is the heater core. If it isn't, than it just condensation on the heater core or in the vents.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||01-16-2001||02:40 AM||||Amazing how others have the same problem I'm having, and before I ask, the question has already been answered!  This place is incredible.<BR>I have been having the exact same symptoms.<BR>Will do the search.  Thanks.<BR>||||reg||6
